1
00:01:05,300 --> 00:01:08,940
=When the Lights Rise=
=Episode 11=

2
00:01:12,820 --> 00:01:13,740
What are you thinking about?

3
00:01:16,580 --> 00:01:17,380
Nothing.

4
00:01:19,380 --> 00:01:20,740
If this wound isn't treated properly,

5
00:01:21,180 --> 00:01:23,220
you might have trouble walking
from now on.

6
00:01:23,620 --> 00:01:25,100
That's my own concern.

7
00:01:25,620 --> 00:01:27,180
Your sister's funeral is tomorrow,
isn't it?

8
00:01:27,420 --> 00:01:29,460
Do you want to be limping
when you see her off?

9
00:01:32,460 --> 00:01:33,500
You don't have to worry.

10
00:01:34,420 --> 00:01:35,420
I won't hurt you.

11
00:01:44,260 --> 00:01:45,500
Go ahead and ask whatever you want.

12
00:01:49,590 --> 00:01:52,380
Did you give me that building?

13
00:01:52,680 --> 00:01:53,140
Yes.

14
00:01:53,820 --> 00:01:54,620
Sign the papers

15
00:01:54,620 --> 00:01:55,820
so I can report back.

16
00:01:56,400 --> 00:01:58,480
(Property Deed)

17
00:01:58,820 --> 00:02:00,700
Are you really buying
this entire building

18
00:02:00,700 --> 00:02:01,740
for Miss Mei?

19
00:02:01,740 --> 00:02:02,420
Don't worry.

20
00:02:02,420 --> 00:02:04,220
You'll still manage the property.

21
00:02:04,390 --> 00:02:05,620
It's just that from now on,

22
00:02:06,020 --> 00:02:07,070
the rent will go to Miss Mei.

23
00:02:07,940 --> 00:02:10,260
Has Miss Mei found herself
a wealthy patron?

24
00:02:10,580 --> 00:02:12,020
Treat Miss Mei well from now on.

25
00:02:12,020 --> 00:02:13,060
Got it.

26
00:02:13,220 --> 00:02:14,260
Come on, sign here.

27
00:02:15,480 --> 00:02:17,120
(Property Deed)

28
00:02:17,420 --> 00:02:18,260
Why?

29
00:02:18,420 --> 00:02:19,260
Consider it

30
00:02:19,540 --> 00:02:20,700
payment for asking you

31
00:02:21,100 --> 00:02:22,580
to help me investigate Xiaozhu's case.

32
00:02:22,660 --> 00:02:23,660
I don't understand.

33
00:02:24,020 --> 00:02:25,580
You've sponsored so many people.

34
00:02:25,780 --> 00:02:27,500
Why do you care so much about Xiaozhu

35
00:02:27,540 --> 00:02:29,060
and go to such lengths to help me?

36
00:02:39,940 --> 00:02:41,180
Xiaozhu was an outstanding student.

37
00:02:42,260 --> 00:02:44,580
Every year, she received

38
00:02:44,580 --> 00:02:45,700
my foundation's top scholarship.

39
00:02:47,260 --> 00:02:48,860
If none of this had happened,

40
00:02:49,620 --> 00:02:52,820
she would have had
a bright future ahead of her.

41
00:02:53,420 --> 00:02:55,580
People have said many things about her.

42
00:02:56,220 --> 00:02:57,660
They focus on who she associated
with outside school,

43
00:02:58,220 --> 00:02:59,420
what she desired,

44
00:02:59,940 --> 00:03:02,620
and the places she visited
before her death.

45
00:03:03,020 --> 00:03:05,740
But hardly anyone cares
about her as a student,

46
00:03:06,340 --> 00:03:07,700
about what she believed,

47
00:03:08,060 --> 00:03:09,540
or what ambitions she had

48
00:03:10,020 --> 00:03:12,700
for the world and the times
she lived in.

49
00:03:13,710 --> 00:03:14,460
You mean

50
00:03:15,620 --> 00:03:17,540
you care about a woman's ambitions?

51
00:03:18,420 --> 00:03:19,220
Of course.

52
00:03:20,420 --> 00:03:21,740
Just like you, Miss Mei.

53
00:03:22,380 --> 00:03:23,380
You dared to investigate the truth

54
00:03:24,220 --> 00:03:25,260
and accuse Lv Mengde openly.

55
00:03:26,260 --> 00:03:27,210
That's your ambition.

56
00:03:28,060 --> 00:03:29,420
A courageous one.

57
00:03:29,620 --> 00:03:31,020
I'm not that noble.

58
00:03:32,260 --> 00:03:33,700
I just want revenge.

59
00:03:35,140 --> 00:03:38,020
I want those who hurt Xiaozhu
to pay with their lives.

60
00:03:42,260 --> 00:03:43,500
Xiaozhu was special.

61
00:03:44,140 --> 00:03:45,220
She was also a thoughtful girl.

62
00:03:45,820 --> 00:03:46,980
Many of her essays

63
00:03:47,460 --> 00:03:48,540
were published
in newspapers and magazines.

64
00:03:52,380 --> 00:03:53,700
On Those Who Share in the Profits.

65
00:03:53,700 --> 00:03:54,740
(On Those Who Share in the Profits)

66
00:03:54,740 --> 00:03:55,660
Have you heard

67
00:03:56,020 --> 00:03:57,820
the claim that women
merely share in the profits?

68
00:03:58,380 --> 00:04:00,380
Xiaozhu once mentioned it to me.

69
00:04:01,420 --> 00:04:04,700
It was said by Liang Qichao.

70
00:04:08,020 --> 00:04:11,180
He argued that women don't
engage in production

71
00:04:11,540 --> 00:04:12,980
or contribute to the economy.

72
00:04:13,580 --> 00:04:16,060
They merely consume
the wealth men produce

73
00:04:16,420 --> 00:04:17,620
and depend on men to support them.

74
00:04:18,620 --> 00:04:21,860
Thus, men treat them
like animals or slaves.

75
00:04:22,780 --> 00:04:23,580
That's right.

76
00:04:24,260 --> 00:04:27,140
Most people generally agree
with Liang's view

77
00:04:28,020 --> 00:04:29,580
that women should receive an education

78
00:04:29,860 --> 00:04:32,420
and become contributors rather
than dependents.

79
00:04:33,020 --> 00:04:34,420
But Xiaozhu disagreed.

80
00:04:34,580 --> 00:04:35,580
She never accepted that view.

81
00:04:38,420 --> 00:04:40,020
(On Those Who Share in the Profits)
Liang cared about women's livelihoods

82
00:04:40,020 --> 00:04:42,420
and hoped all women could
receive an education

83
00:04:42,420 --> 00:04:43,780
so they could join the workforce

84
00:04:43,780 --> 00:04:44,820
and contribute to economic production.

85
00:04:45,050 --> 00:04:47,140
His intentions were indeed fair-minded,

86
00:04:47,140 --> 00:04:48,420
and his vision looked a century ahead.

87
00:04:48,620 --> 00:04:49,780
But women in traditional roles

88
00:04:49,780 --> 00:04:51,060
are not merely dependent on others.

89
00:04:51,620 --> 00:04:54,100
Without their contributions
to household production,

90
00:04:54,180 --> 00:04:56,380
social production would come
to a standstill,

91
00:04:56,580 --> 00:04:57,820
and efficiency would decline.

92
00:04:58,420 --> 00:05:00,900
What truly needs to change
isn't just women,

93
00:05:01,420 --> 00:05:03,220
but also society's definition
of economic value

94
00:05:03,420 --> 00:05:04,660
and its understanding of gender.

95
00:05:05,820 --> 00:05:06,780
She was remarkable.

96
00:05:07,380 --> 00:05:08,940
She never blindly accepted
others' views.

97
00:05:09,420 --> 00:05:10,660
She dared to break free of constraints

98
00:05:11,020 --> 00:05:12,060
and challenge authority.

99
00:05:12,420 --> 00:05:13,500
She thought for herself.

100
00:05:13,940 --> 00:05:15,180
I was her sponsor.

101
00:05:16,020 --> 00:05:17,100
I want to prove

102
00:05:17,380 --> 00:05:19,260
that the outstanding student
sponsored by my Cishan Foundation

103
00:05:19,460 --> 00:05:21,100
wasn't the kind of girl people claimed,

104
00:05:21,540 --> 00:05:22,660
someone who depended on men

105
00:05:22,980 --> 00:05:25,060
and lost her way
in pursuit of wealth and status.

106
00:05:25,940 --> 00:05:26,740
What's more,

107
00:05:27,380 --> 00:05:28,740
there are probably many other victims

108
00:05:29,860 --> 00:05:30,860
just like her.

109
00:05:30,940 --> 00:05:31,740
Many?

110
00:05:48,160 --> 00:05:49,910
Yiyi, are you asleep?

111
00:05:50,340 --> 00:05:51,380
Come in.

112
00:05:54,980 --> 00:05:55,940
Did I wake you?

113
00:05:56,500 --> 00:05:57,980
Since you're awake, have some porridge.

114
00:05:58,140 --> 00:05:58,700
Here.

115
00:06:00,140 --> 00:06:00,820
Take it away.

116
00:06:00,820 --> 00:06:01,860
I'm not eating.

117
00:06:02,210 --> 00:06:03,160
You can be angry,

118
00:06:03,780 --> 00:06:04,780
but you can't starve yourself.

119
00:06:04,900 --> 00:06:06,460
I'm not starving myself.

120
00:06:14,220 --> 00:06:15,180
What are you doing?

121
00:06:16,420 --> 00:06:17,860
I'll just ask a few questions and leave.

122
00:06:18,980 --> 00:06:19,860
What I promised you,

123
00:06:19,860 --> 00:06:21,140
I'll still do.

124
00:06:26,660 --> 00:06:27,980
Where have you been these past few days?

125
00:06:29,180 --> 00:06:30,260
Nanyang Hotel.

126
00:06:30,380 --> 00:06:31,420
What were you doing there?

127
00:06:35,420 --> 00:06:36,620
I can tell you,

128
00:06:38,060 --> 00:06:39,580
but don't tell Miss Mei.

129
00:06:43,720 --> 00:06:44,880
I'm not the one asking you
to keep it secret.

130
00:06:44,880 --> 00:06:45,660
It's Kuang Yijie.

131
00:06:47,610 --> 00:06:48,620
Kuang Yijie?

132
00:06:50,020 --> 00:06:51,620
Why did he take you to a hotel?

133
00:06:53,800 --> 00:06:57,580
That day, I went to the Kuang residence
to see Mengde.

134
00:06:59,380 --> 00:07:00,940
And I ran into him at the entrance.

135
00:07:09,340 --> 00:07:10,260
Ding Yiyi.

136
00:07:12,220 --> 00:07:13,020
It's you.

137
00:07:13,540 --> 00:07:14,620
Are you here to see my uncle?

138
00:07:14,740 --> 00:07:15,700
That's none of your business.

139
00:07:16,540 --> 00:07:17,420
We were classmates, after all.

140
00:07:17,940 --> 00:07:18,940
I'll help you.

141
00:07:20,220 --> 00:07:21,140
What do you mean?

142
00:07:21,580 --> 00:07:22,460
To tell you the truth,

143
00:07:23,180 --> 00:07:24,900
having a classmate become my aunt

144
00:07:25,380 --> 00:07:26,550
would be rather strange.

145
00:07:27,340 --> 00:07:29,060
But I'm not so old-fashioned.

146
00:07:31,420 --> 00:07:33,260
If you really want to marry my uncle,

147
00:07:34,340 --> 00:07:35,620
I can put in

148
00:07:35,620 --> 00:07:36,900
a good word for you with my grandfather.

149
00:07:39,100 --> 00:07:39,900
Really?

150
00:07:40,020 --> 00:07:41,300
Would you really help me?

151
00:07:41,460 --> 00:07:42,260
Of course.

152
00:07:43,180 --> 00:07:45,980
But my family's had
a lot going on lately.

153
00:07:46,780 --> 00:07:48,140
You'd better wait
until things settle down.

154
00:07:48,180 --> 00:07:50,060
Then could you let me see Mengde first?

155
00:07:50,220 --> 00:07:51,060
Tell him

156
00:07:51,060 --> 00:07:52,420
I promise I won't bother him.

157
00:07:52,740 --> 00:07:54,180
I just want to see him.

158
00:07:54,340 --> 00:07:55,780
My uncle's been rather busy lately.

159
00:07:56,020 --> 00:07:57,580
I really won't bother him.

160
00:07:58,180 --> 00:07:59,820
I can help him with so many things.

161
00:07:59,820 --> 00:08:00,620
I can...

162
00:08:05,460 --> 00:08:06,620
Are you feeling unwell?

163
00:08:09,020 --> 00:08:10,380
You look so worn out.

164
00:08:11,180 --> 00:08:12,660
My uncle would be upset
to see you like this.

165
00:08:21,140 --> 00:08:23,220
Yiyi, we had an agreement.

166
00:08:23,380 --> 00:08:24,500
See a doctor now,

167
00:08:25,060 --> 00:08:26,460
and we'll decide what to do afterward.

168
00:08:28,260 --> 00:08:30,060
What are you seeing Dr. Bai about?

169
00:08:32,620 --> 00:08:33,700
That's private.

170
00:08:34,380 --> 00:08:36,220
Let's wait until we see Dr. Bai.

171
00:08:37,020 --> 00:08:37,940
Follow me.

172
00:08:40,540 --> 00:08:41,340
Go on.

173
00:08:53,380 --> 00:08:54,980
You'll wait outside for me, right?

174
00:08:55,820 --> 00:08:57,100
I'll be right here waiting for you.

175
00:09:19,020 --> 00:09:20,060
What's troubling you?

176
00:09:21,460 --> 00:09:22,980
I heard from Kuang Yijie

177
00:09:23,460 --> 00:09:25,500
that you've treated
many dance hostesses.

178
00:09:26,180 --> 00:09:27,020
For free.

179
00:09:27,020 --> 00:09:28,160
Do you work at a dance hall?

180
00:09:28,240 --> 00:09:29,050
No.

181
00:09:31,060 --> 00:09:32,020
I just

182
00:09:34,180 --> 00:09:35,140
went there to take a look.

183
00:09:35,140 --> 00:09:36,380
Let me examine you.

184
00:09:41,260 --> 00:09:41,860
Anyway,

185
00:09:41,860 --> 00:09:43,980
he took me to the hospital
to see a doctor.

186
00:09:45,140 --> 00:09:47,140
Then he found out
I'd had a falling-out with my family,

187
00:09:47,860 --> 00:09:50,060
so he arranged for me
to stay at the hotel.

188
00:09:52,340 --> 00:09:53,260
Once the farewell banquet was over,

189
00:09:53,260 --> 00:09:54,300
he brought me home.

190
00:09:54,620 --> 00:09:56,380
He just brought you home
out of the blue?

191
00:09:56,660 --> 00:09:57,900
Nothing else happened?

192
00:10:03,280 --> 00:10:05,120
(Doctor's Office)

193
00:10:07,220 --> 00:10:08,020
Yiyi.

194
00:10:08,980 --> 00:10:09,660
Let go of me.

195
00:10:09,980 --> 00:10:11,420
Did the examination reveal something?

196
00:10:11,420 --> 00:10:12,780
No.

197
00:10:12,780 --> 00:10:13,660
You know

198
00:10:14,140 --> 00:10:15,300
I'm the only person

199
00:10:15,300 --> 00:10:15,980
you can rely on now.

200
00:10:16,220 --> 00:10:17,500
You have to tell me what's going on

201
00:10:17,500 --> 00:10:18,660
before I can help you.

202
00:10:22,660 --> 00:10:23,220
Promise me

203
00:10:25,140 --> 00:10:26,340
you won't tell anyone.

204
00:10:26,500 --> 00:10:27,220
I promise.

205
00:10:36,140 --> 00:10:36,940
No.

206
00:10:42,620 --> 00:10:44,300
He told me to listen to you

207
00:10:44,860 --> 00:10:46,180
and also

208
00:10:46,460 --> 00:10:48,620
invited me to Mei Xiaozhu's funeral.

209
00:10:48,860 --> 00:10:51,300
He invited you to Mei Xiaozhu's funeral?

210
00:10:52,620 --> 00:10:54,180
He was very close to Mei Xiaozhu?

211
00:10:54,620 --> 00:10:55,980
I think he liked her.

212
00:10:57,260 --> 00:10:58,900
I often saw them together,

213
00:10:58,900 --> 00:11:00,300
whispering to each other.

214
00:11:01,350 --> 00:11:03,620
She'd already caught
the eye of a young master,

215
00:11:04,820 --> 00:11:06,460
yet she still insisted
on competing with me.

216
00:11:53,220 --> 00:11:53,820
Young Master.

217
00:11:53,820 --> 00:11:54,260
It's so late.

218
00:11:54,260 --> 00:11:55,220
What brings you here?

219
00:11:55,420 --> 00:11:56,340
I came to get something.

220
00:11:56,380 --> 00:11:57,460
Carry on with your meal and drinks.

221
00:11:57,620 --> 00:11:59,700
All right. Come on, everyone.

222
00:11:59,700 --> 00:12:00,360
Let's get back to eating.

223
00:12:00,360 --> 00:12:00,800
All right.

224
00:12:20,940 --> 00:12:21,740
Father.

225
00:12:21,980 --> 00:12:23,380
Everything is ready.

226
00:12:24,020 --> 00:12:26,020
Please begin at the scheduled time.

227
00:12:26,300 --> 00:12:27,300
I understand.

228
00:12:28,180 --> 00:12:31,620
Thank you for your help, Mr. Jing.

229
00:12:31,900 --> 00:12:34,340
I'm the one who should
thank you, Father.

230
00:12:34,500 --> 00:12:37,380
This is simply my duty.

231
00:12:41,020 --> 00:12:41,980
I know.

232
00:12:42,660 --> 00:12:44,100
You wouldn't have wanted this funeral.

233
00:12:45,060 --> 00:12:46,500
Just pretend no one else is here.

234
00:12:47,070 --> 00:12:48,040
It's just me, your sister.

235
00:12:48,750 --> 00:12:51,420
I'll stay with you until the very end.

236
00:12:56,420 --> 00:12:59,060
Didn't you say last night
you weren't going to the funeral?

237
00:12:59,340 --> 00:13:01,380
Ultimately, this matter concerns
the Kuang family.

238
00:13:01,980 --> 00:13:03,620
Since your grandfather
refuses to attend,

239
00:13:04,020 --> 00:13:05,620
I should naturally represent the family.

240
00:13:05,980 --> 00:13:06,940
If you're willing to go,

241
00:13:07,380 --> 00:13:08,620
that would be for the best.

242
00:13:08,850 --> 00:13:10,100
This show

243
00:13:10,460 --> 00:13:12,260
mustn't end so soon.

244
00:13:27,380 --> 00:13:28,240
It's been seven years.

245
00:13:31,140 --> 00:13:31,980
Come in.

246
00:13:38,620 --> 00:13:39,900
Offer some incense to Mom and Dad.

247
00:14:01,420 --> 00:14:03,080
Are you really coming
to the funeral with me?

248
00:14:03,080 --> 00:14:04,160
(Memorial Tablet of My Late Father Ding Qian.
Memorial Tablet of My Late Mother Li Qiaozhen)

249
00:14:04,820 --> 00:14:05,780
We were classmates, after all.

250
00:14:06,660 --> 00:14:07,940
I should go and say goodbye.

251
00:14:19,780 --> 00:14:20,420
Father.

252
00:14:23,820 --> 00:14:25,580
Miss Mei, my condolences.

253
00:14:28,180 --> 00:14:31,380
Miss Mei is overwhelmed with grief.

254
00:14:31,540 --> 00:14:34,500
I hope Mr. Yoshida will understand.

255
00:14:36,620 --> 00:14:37,900
Of course.

256
00:14:38,020 --> 00:14:38,820
All right.

257
00:14:38,860 --> 00:14:40,300
Father, let's go inside.

258
00:14:52,700 --> 00:14:53,660
Zhao, I'll wait for you inside.

259
00:15:01,660 --> 00:15:02,700
Didn't we agree

260
00:15:03,020 --> 00:15:04,620
that you wouldn't get involved
in this mess?

261
00:15:04,740 --> 00:15:06,660
I think I know who that older sister is.

262
00:15:09,380 --> 00:15:10,500
She should be here already.

263
00:15:20,220 --> 00:15:20,900
Mengde.

264
00:15:22,740 --> 00:15:23,540
Mengde.

265
00:15:23,620 --> 00:15:25,340
I got the note you sent me.

266
00:15:35,540 --> 00:15:36,460
I never expected

267
00:15:36,620 --> 00:15:38,340
the Kuang family to attend the funeral.

268
00:15:38,940 --> 00:15:39,740
Well,

269
00:15:40,180 --> 00:15:42,700
they have to show
the Kun Society some respect.

270
00:15:43,670 --> 00:15:44,940
With such an important occasion,

271
00:15:44,940 --> 00:15:47,380
why aren't Boss Kuang
and his illegitimate son here?

272
00:15:47,380 --> 00:15:48,540
How would they dare show their faces?

273
00:15:48,780 --> 00:15:50,980
At Boss Dong's farewell banquet,

274
00:15:51,700 --> 00:15:53,220
that woman surnamed Mei
pulled out a knife

275
00:15:53,220 --> 00:15:54,500
and nearly killed him.

276
00:15:55,860 --> 00:15:56,820
After all,

277
00:15:57,020 --> 00:15:58,580
if this hadn't become such
a huge scandal,

278
00:15:58,730 --> 00:15:59,860
could she have afforded

279
00:15:59,860 --> 00:16:01,280
such a lavish funeral for her sister?

280
00:16:01,280 --> 00:16:02,220
The way I see it,

281
00:16:02,220 --> 00:16:04,500
all this commotion has turned out
for the best.

282
00:16:04,620 --> 00:16:06,420
Our Civil Affairs Bureau
gets some credit too.

283
00:16:06,420 --> 00:16:07,620
My sister's funeral

284
00:16:09,980 --> 00:16:11,980
isn't an opportunity
to make anyone look good.

285
00:16:12,220 --> 00:16:14,300
Come on, that's hardly fair.

286
00:16:14,340 --> 00:16:15,060
Whatever you say,

287
00:16:15,060 --> 00:16:15,900
we did contribute money...

288
00:16:15,900 --> 00:16:16,660
I don't need it.

289
00:16:17,900 --> 00:16:18,580
Besides,

290
00:16:20,020 --> 00:16:21,180
Xiaozhu wouldn't want to see

291
00:16:21,180 --> 00:16:22,540
hypocrites like you here either.

292
00:16:37,740 --> 00:16:38,860
Where did Ding Yiyi go?

293
00:16:39,660 --> 00:16:40,820
She said she was going to the restroom.

294
00:16:40,820 --> 00:16:42,060
But I sent someone in to check,

295
00:16:42,260 --> 00:16:43,060
and she wasn't there.

296
00:16:45,220 --> 00:16:46,060
Normally,

297
00:16:46,620 --> 00:16:48,060
she wouldn't have come
to the funeral willingly.

298
00:16:48,180 --> 00:16:49,540
Could she have arranged to meet someone?

299
00:16:51,420 --> 00:16:53,220
I also thought she was acting strangely.

300
00:16:55,970 --> 00:16:59,010
♪And watch the lights
come on one by one♪

301
00:16:59,570 --> 00:17:02,410
♪Like blades cutting
through the radiance♪

302
00:17:03,050 --> 00:17:05,890
♪You may treat me as dust
beneath your feet♪

303
00:17:05,890 --> 00:17:07,810
♪Or wipe me away like ashes♪

304
00:17:07,810 --> 00:17:09,370
♪Leaving a cold ending♪

305
00:17:09,370 --> 00:17:11,330
♪But I refuse to fall♪

306
00:17:11,330 --> 00:17:16,250
♪I refuse to become a shadow
fading beneath the lights♪

307
00:17:16,370 --> 00:17:18,810
♪I refuse to dissolve into♪

308
00:17:19,890 --> 00:17:22,890
♪The lifeless light of the past♪

309
00:17:23,210 --> 00:17:26,050
♪I want sharpness at my fingertips♪

310
00:17:26,090 --> 00:17:28,890
♪And steps that avoid
the traps among the thorns♪

311
00:17:29,610 --> 00:17:32,490
♪At dawn, I will look
straight into your eyes♪

312
00:17:32,490 --> 00:17:35,690
♪My gaze clear, illuminating the dawn♪

313
00:17:37,170 --> 00:17:39,930
♪Those who have hurt me♪

314
00:17:40,490 --> 00:17:43,170
♪I choose to pierce through♪

315
00:17:44,770 --> 00:17:46,250
♪To tear apart♪

316
00:17:46,370 --> 00:17:52,250
♪To ignite a sacred flame♪

317
00:17:53,930 --> 00:17:56,050
♪I do not pray to the gods♪

318
00:17:56,050 --> 00:17:58,970
♪Nor bow to power♪

319
00:17:58,970 --> 00:18:01,250
♪I will no longer play the tragic lead♪

320
00:18:03,050 --> 00:18:06,970
♪I will stand and carve
the path of my own fate♪
